  "notes": "Generic sheer curtain, not a specific product: one panel of a white voile curtain on a ceiling track, pulled open to the side of a window, where it gathers into a stack of tight wave folds with a double hem and a heading tape. Place it beside a window: like other floor items it snaps flush and square to the wall, also to the angled glazing walls, and its folds keep 3 cm off it. It stands on the floor so it can snap to the wall and reaches the ceiling with its track (255 cm, the apartment's ceiling height); the cloth ends 1.5 cm above the floor. It is one panel, 36.6 cm wide and 15.3 cm deep including the gap at the back: duplicate it for the other side of the window. Only the folds collide, not the gap behind them. The voile is half transparent (curtain.voile-white, opacity 0.5): the window frame, the railing and whatever stands behind show through it, less where the folds overlap and at the hem and heading, where the cloth is double. curtain.voile-light-blue is the same voile in light blue; any curtain or fabric preset can be picked."
